 "change": "copyPixels' fully-known-target branch, when source and target storages differ (little-endian only), processes four pixels per step in separate loops for keyed (forward or mirrored) and unkeyed mirrored copies: raw pointers stepped without overflow checks, the key constants hoisted, the 24-bit key test per lane; a group the key rejects entirely is skipped (no load or store), one it accepts entirely is stored without reading the target, a mixed group stores the rejected lanes' target values back unchanged. The row's remainder and same-surface copies stay scalar. R4a (the first version: per-group offsets with overflow checks, branches inside the loop, always loading and storing the target) was slower and is parked (rt-r4a-simd-copies-parked-20261010.json)",
